  "id": "proprioception",
  "term": "proprioception",
  "definition": "Proprioception is the body’s sense of where its parts are and how they are moving. It comes from signals from receptors in muscles, tendons, joints, and the inner ear that are sent to the central nervous system, helping support movement awareness and postural balance.",
